<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" version="1.1" creator="Perplexity Computer">
  <metadata>
    <name>Jindabyne to Mansfield - Sun 8 to Wed 11 Nov 2026 - 4 days - V2</name>
    <desc>Trip dates Sun 8 - Wed 11 Nov 2026. Planned track, not field or DMD2-device tested. Check current closures, weather, access signs and fuel availability before departure. Map geometry (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright</desc>
    <keywords>adventure motorcycle,GPX track,Victoria,High Country,gravel</keywords>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-36.415039" lon="148.611061">
    <name>Jindabyne START - Barry Way</name>
    <desc>Fuel in Jindabyne before departure. Plan for 200 km to Omeo; this track bypasses Benambra township.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.952929" lon="148.325479">
    <name>Limestone Road junction</name>
    <desc>Turn west from Snowy River Road onto Limestone Road. Remote narrow gravel sections.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.972699" lon="147.726661">
    <name>Old McLeinster Road</name>
    <desc>Unsealed connection towards Benambra Road; Benambra fuel is NOT on this track.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.098696" lon="147.594303">
    <name>Omeo OVERNIGHT - Day Avenue</name>
    <desc>Town stop on Day Avenue, not an exact hotel doorstep. Overnight Sun 8 Nov: Golden Age Hotel, 189 Day Ave, 03 5159 1344 (not booked). Refuel for Day 2.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.098696" lon="147.594303">
    <name>Omeo START - Day Avenue</name>
    <desc>Fill here. Allow 175 km plus reserve to Dargo. Do not rely on alpine-village fuel.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.210411" lon="147.510070">
    <name>Birregun Road</name>
    <desc>Forest-road approach via Cassilis and Upper Livingstone Road.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.233843" lon="147.380343">
    <name>Dogs Grave access</name>
    <desc>Short access along Dogs Grave Track. Historic grave nearby; stop and locate on foot. Return along the same track and Birregun Road to the Dinner Plain Track turnoff.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.021044" lon="147.235085">
    <name>Dinner Plain - Great Alpine Road</name>
    <desc>End of Dinner Plain Track. Seasonal 4WD route, not all smooth gravel. Continue west on the sealed Great Alpine Road to Dargo High Plains Road.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.097174" lon="147.053459">
    <name>Blue Rag trig approach - TURNAROUND</name>
    <desc>Difficult exposed rocky track, experienced riders in suitable dry conditions only. Return to Dargo High Plains Road along the same Blue Rag track, about 14 km return.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.461624" lon="147.251071">
    <name>Dargo OVERNIGHT</name>
    <desc>Overnight Mon 9 Nov: Dargo Hotel, 03 5140 1231 (not booked). Fill at Dargo General Store before 6 pm Monday.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.461600" lon="147.251400">
    <name>Dargo START</name>
    <desc>Fuel - last until Licola (127 km).</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Green</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.404400" lon="147.084100">
    <name>Billy Goat Bluff Track</name>
    <desc>Start of the climb: one of Victoria's steepest 4WD tracks - about 1200 m ascent in 7 km with rocky steps, climbed one-way to the Pinnacles. Seasonal closures scheduled to lift 29 Oct 2026 - recheck Parks Victoria before riding.</desc>
    <sym>Danger</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.460300" lon="147.055300">
    <name>The Pinnacles</name>
    <desc>Picnic area and car park at the top of the climb - short steep walk up to the fire tower lookout (no vehicle access to the tower).</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.627000" lon="146.624000">
    <name>Licola</name>
    <desc>Refuel here Tue 10 Nov - Licola Village Store, listed 8:30 am-4:30 pm daily, 0487 800 121. Jamieson also has a servo but with unreliable hours - confirm opening if you plan to use it. If Jamieson fuel is unavailable, plan for about 245 km through to Mansfield. Confirm trading hours.</desc>
    <sym>Fuel</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.299500" lon="146.136000">
    <name>Jamieson FINISH</name>
    <desc>Overnight Tue 10 Nov: Courthouse Hotel, cnr Perkins and Nash St, 03 5777 0503 (not booked - confirm). Fuel: Jamieson Service Station, 9 Perkins St - reported unreliable hours, do not rely on it.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Red</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.299500" lon="146.136000">
    <name>Jamieson START</name>
    <desc>Top up at Licola yesterday. Jamieson Service Station (9 Perkins St) has fuel but unreliable hours - do not count on it. Next reliable fuel is Mansfield, 245 km after Licola.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Green</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.223000" lon="146.310000">
    <name>Sheepyard Flat</name>
    <desc>Howqua River camping area.</desc>
    <sym>Camping</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.110200" lon="146.533500">
    <name>Craig's Hut parking</name>
    <desc>Vehicle access area at the end of Clear Hills Track - short walk to the hut. Rocky 4WD track, take care on a big bike. Do not continue up Clear Hills Track towards the Mt Stirling summit - that section is closed until about 1 Dec.</desc>
    <sym>Tunnel</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.113300" lon="146.464000">
    <name>Telephone Box Junction</name>
    <desc>Junction of Stirling and Circuit Rds (King's Saddle area) on the ride down. Seasonal closures + resort rules can apply - check signage.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.110500" lon="146.399700">
    <name>Mirimbah</name>
    <desc>Base of Mt Buller.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Yellow</sym>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.052000" lon="146.088500">
    <name>Mansfield FINISH</name>
    <desc>Town centre - fuel + everything.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Red</sym>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Day 1 - Sun 8 Nov 2026 - Jindabyne to Omeo via Barry Way and Limestone Road</name>
    <desc>199.3 km. Surface audit: 68.8% tagged unsealed, 31.2% sealed.</desc>
